IMPORT prelude

-- Maintenance Orders (Reciprocal Enforcement) Act 1975 (Singapore) -- which orders the Act reaches (s 2 "maintenance order",
-- s 17(2)), sending a Singapore order abroad (s 3), the provisional order against a payer abroad (ss 4, 5(3)), registering and
-- confirming a foreign order in Singapore (ss 6, 7), enforcement, the change-of-address offence and the date from which sums run
-- (s 8(4), (7), (8)), varying and revoking a registered order (s 9(2)-(4), (9)), cancelling registration (s 10), compensation of
-- witnesses (s 14(3)) and currency conversion (s 16(2), (5)).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/MOREA1975.txt. The cover says it "incorporates all
-- amendments up to and including 1 December 2021 and comes into operation on 31 December 2021"; every page is headed "Informal
-- Consolidation - version in force from 16/1/2025". The latest amendment annotated is Act 18 of 2023 (Family Justice Reform Act
-- 2023, commencement 16 January 2025), which deleted s 8(2) and (3). SSO's metadata calls it the "Current version as at 01 Oct 2026".
-- The arrangement of sections at the top of the deposit is out of step with the body (it omits "Appeals" as s 12); the body's
-- numbering is followed here.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Chosen for its everyday-life relevance: it is how a wife, former wife or child in Singapore gets a maintenance
-- order enforced against a payer who has moved to a reciprocating country, and how a foreign order is enforced against a payer
-- living in Singapore. SCOPED to what a payer or payee meets. Not encoded: the documents the court officer and the Minister send
-- (ss 3(3), 4(4), 6(2), 11) beyond the conditions for sending them; Singapore's retained jurisdiction (s 3(4)); confirmation of
-- foreign provisional variation and revocation orders (ss 5(5), (6), (9), 9(6), (7)); appeals (s 12); evidence and proof of
-- foreign documents (ss 13, 14(1), (2), (4), 15); the manner of payment (s 16(1)); the list of reciprocating countries (made by
-- Gazette notification under s 17(1), none retrieved); rules, regulations and transitional provisions (ss 18, 18A, 19).
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text, following the conventions of the example naive rows. No pipeline, no coverage
-- table, no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Maintenance Orders (Reciprocal Enforcement) Act 1975 -- maintenance`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the earlier of` MEANS IF `a` AT MOST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

§§ `2 -- what is a maintenance order`

-- s 2 "maintenance order": "(a) an order (including an affiliation order or order consequent upon an affiliation order) which
-- provides for the payment of a lump sum or the making of periodical payments -- (i) by a man towards the maintenance of his wife
-- or former wife; or (ii) by a person towards the maintenance of the person's child; and (b) an affiliation order or order
-- consequent upon an affiliation order, being an order which provides for the payment by a person adjudged, found or declared to be
-- a child's father of expenses incidental to the child's birth or, where the child had died, of the child's funeral expenses".
-- "affiliation order": an order adjudging a person to be the father of a child, "whether or not it also provides for the
-- maintenance of the child".
-- Spousal maintenance is reached only when a MAN pays his wife or former wife. Child maintenance is reached whoever pays. An order
-- for an adult child to maintain a parent is not within either limb. A bare paternity finding with no payment is not within either.
DECLARE Order IS ONE OF
    `monthly maintenance by a man to his wife`
    `a lump sum by a man to his former wife`
    `monthly maintenance by a woman to her husband`
    `monthly maintenance by a woman to her former husband`
    `monthly maintenance by a father to his child`
    `monthly maintenance by a mother to her child`
    `birth expenses payable by an adjudged father`
    `funeral expenses of a child payable by an adjudged father`
    `a bare finding of paternity`
    `maintenance of a parent by an adult child`

GIVEN `the order` IS AN Order
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a maintenance order under the Act` IF
    CONSIDER `the order`
    WHEN `monthly maintenance by a woman to her husband` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `monthly maintenance by a woman to her former husband` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a bare finding of paternity` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `maintenance of a parent by an adult child` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `3, 17(2) -- sending a Singapore order abroad`

-- s 3(1): "Where the payer under a maintenance order made, whether before or after 3 May 1976, by a court in Singapore is residing in
-- a reciprocating country, the payee under the order may apply for the order to be sent to that country for enforcement."
-- s 17(2): a country designated "otherwise than as regards maintenance orders generally is ... taken to be a reciprocating country
-- only as regards maintenance orders of the class to which the designation extends".
GIVEN `the order` IS AN Order, `made by a court in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN, `payer resides in a designated country` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the designation extends to this class of order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the payee may apply to send the order abroad` IF
        `is a maintenance order under the Act` `the order`
    AND `made by a court in Singapore`
    AND `payer resides in a designated country`
    AND `the designation extends to this class of order`

§§ `4 -- a provisional order against a payer abroad`

-- s 4(1): where a complaint is made to a Family Court "against a person residing in a reciprocating country" and the court would
-- have jurisdiction to make a maintenance order if "(a) that person were residing in Singapore; and (b) a summons ... had been duly
-- served on that person", the court has jurisdiction and may make the order. (2): such an order "is a provisional order".
-- s 2 "provisional order": "provisional only and has no effect unless confirmed, with or without alteration, by a competent court
-- in a reciprocating country". s 4(5): once confirmed it is treated "as if the order had never been a provisional order".
GIVEN `respondent resides in a reciprocating country` IS A BOOLEAN, `court would have jurisdiction if respondent resided and was served` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Family Court may hear the complaint under section 4` IF
    `respondent resides in a reciprocating country` AND `court would have jurisdiction if respondent resided and was served`

GIVEN `made under section 4` IS A BOOLEAN, `confirmed by a competent court abroad` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Singapore order has effect` IF
    (NOT `made under section 4`) OR `confirmed by a competent court abroad`

§§ `5(3) -- increasing a Singapore order that has gone abroad`

-- s 5(3): where the court "proposes to vary it by increasing the rate of the payments under the order, the order varying that order
-- is a provisional order unless either -- (a) both the payer and the payee under the order appear in the proceedings; or (b) the
-- applicant appears and the appropriate process has been duly served on the other party". (2): the court "has power" to vary any
-- such order by a provisional order -- a power, not a requirement, for any other variation.
GIVEN `increases the rate` IS A BOOLEAN, `both parties appear` IS A BOOLEAN, `the applicant appears` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `process duly served on the other party` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the variation must be provisional` IF
        `increases the rate`
    AND (NOT `both parties appear`)
    AND (NOT (`the applicant appears` AND `process duly served on the other party`))

§§ `6 -- registering a foreign order in Singapore`

-- s 6(1): applies to an order made by a court in a reciprocating country, "including such an order ... which has been confirmed by
-- a court in another reciprocating country but excluding a provisional order which has not been confirmed".
-- (2): the Minister sends it to the court officer if "it appears to the Minister that the payer under the order is residing in
-- Singapore"; (3): the officer "must, subject to subsection (4), register the order"; (4): if the officer "is satisfied that the
-- payer is not so residing" within the court's jurisdiction, the copy is returned to the Minister.
GIVEN `a provisional order` IS A BOOLEAN, `confirmed by a court in another reciprocating country` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `payer appears to the Minister to reside in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN, `officer satisfied payer does not reside within the jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the officer must register the foreign order` IF
        ((NOT `a provisional order`) OR `confirmed by a court in another reciprocating country`)
    AND `payer appears to the Minister to reside in Singapore`
    AND (NOT `officer satisfied payer does not reside within the jurisdiction`)

§§ `7 -- confirming a foreign provisional order`

-- s 7(2): the court is to "(c) if the payer under the order establishes any grounds on which the payer might have opposed the making
-- of the order in the proceedings in which the order was made -- refuse to confirm the order; and (d) in any other case -- confirm
-- the order either without alteration or with such alterations as it thinks reasonable". (3): the foreign court's statement of the
-- grounds "is conclusive evidence that the payer might have opposed the making of the order on any of those grounds".
-- (5): if confirmed, the officer must register it; if refused, return the papers to the Minister. (6): if "a summons to appear ...
-- cannot be duly served on the payer", the papers go back to the Minister with a statement of the payer's whereabouts.
DECLARE Outcome IS ONE OF
    `returned to the Minister unheard`
    `refused and returned to the Minister`
    `confirmed and registered`

GIVEN `summons can be served on the payer` IS A BOOLEAN, `payer establishes a ground of opposition` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN Outcome
`the confirmation outcome` MEANS
    IF NOT `summons can be served on the payer`
    THEN `returned to the Minister unheard`
    ELSE IF `payer establishes a ground of opposition`
         THEN `refused and returned to the Minister`
         ELSE `confirmed and registered`

§§ `8(4) -- telling the court of a change of address`

-- s 8(4): "Any person for the time being under an obligation to make payments pursuant to a registered order must give notice of any
-- change of address to the clerk of the registering court, and any person failing without reasonable excuse to give such a notice
-- shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $500." No imprisonment is provided.
GIVEN `obliged to pay under a registered order` IS A BOOLEAN, `changed address` IS A BOOLEAN, `notified the clerk` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `had a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `commits the change-of-address offence` IF
        `obliged to pay under a registered order`
    AND `changed address`
    AND (NOT `notified the clerk`)
    AND (NOT `had a reasonable excuse`)

`the maximum fine for the change-of-address offence` MEANS 500

§§ `8(7), (8) -- from when sums are payable`

-- s 8(7): "Subject to subsection (8), sums of money payable under a registered order are payable in accordance with the order as from
-- the date on which the order was made." (8): the court confirming a provisional order under s 7 may direct that sums are payable
-- "as from such date (being a date later than the date on which the order was made) as it may specify".
-- Days are counted from any fixed origin. A direction naming a date not later than the order date is outside (8) and is ignored.
GIVEN `day the order was made` IS A NUMBER, `confirmed under section 7` IS A BOOLEAN, `day directed by the confirming court` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the day sums are payable from` MEANS
    IF `confirmed under section 7` AND `day directed by the confirming court` GREATER THAN `day the order was made`
    THEN `day directed by the confirming court`
    ELSE `day the order was made`

§§ `9(2)-(4) -- varying and revoking a registered order`

-- s 9(2): "The registering court is not to vary a registered order otherwise than by a provisional order unless -- (a) both the payer
-- and the payee under the registered order are for the time being residing in Singapore; (b) the application is made by the payee
-- under the registered order; or (c) the variation consists of a reduction in the rate of the payments under the registered order
-- and is made solely on the ground that there has been a change in the financial circumstances of the payer since the registered
-- order was made or ... confirmed, and the courts in the reciprocating country in which the maintenance order in question was made
-- do not have power ... to confirm provisional orders varying maintenance orders."
-- A payee's application may be decided outright wherever the parties live; a payer's application for a reduction may not, unless
-- the foreign courts cannot confirm provisional variations.
GIVEN `both parties reside in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN, `applied for by the payee` IS A BOOLEAN, `a reduction` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `solely on a change in the payer's finances` IS A BOOLEAN, `foreign courts can confirm provisional variations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the registering court may vary outright` IF
        `both parties reside in Singapore`
    OR  `applied for by the payee`
    OR  (`a reduction` AND `solely on a change in the payer's finances` AND (NOT `foreign courts can confirm provisional variations`))

-- s 9(3): "The registering court is not to revoke a registered order otherwise than by a provisional order unless both the payer and
-- the payee under the registered order are for the time being residing in Singapore."
GIVEN `both parties reside in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the registering court may revoke outright` IF
    `both parties reside in Singapore`

-- s 9(4): on revocation, unless both reside in Singapore, the court "is to apply the law applied by the reciprocating country in
-- which the registered order was made", and may make a provisional order "if it has reason to believe that the ground ... is a
-- ground on which the order could be revoked according to the law applied by the reciprocating country, even though it has not
-- been established that it is such a ground".
GIVEN `both parties reside in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the court applies the foreign country's law on revocation` IF
    NOT `both parties reside in Singapore`

GIVEN `both parties reside in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN, `ground established under the foreign law` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `reason to believe the ground is good under the foreign law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the court may make a provisional revocation order` IF
        (NOT `both parties reside in Singapore`)
    AND (`ground established under the foreign law` OR `reason to believe the ground is good under the foreign law`)

§§ `9(9), 10 -- arrears survive revocation; cancelling registration`

-- s 9(9): a revoked registered order is deemed, from the date the revocation takes effect, "to have ceased to have effect except as
-- respects any arrears due under the registered order at that date". s 10(1): on cancellation "any arrears due ... continue to be
-- recoverable as if the registration had not been cancelled".
-- A sum falling due ON the date the revocation takes effect is treated as "due at that date" (an inference; the text does not say).
GIVEN `day the instalment fell due` IS A NUMBER, `day revocation takes effect` IS A NUMBER, `instalment paid` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the instalment is still recoverable` IF
        `day the instalment fell due` AT MOST `day revocation takes effect`
    AND (NOT `instalment paid`)

-- s 10(1): the officer "must cancel the registration" where the order is revoked by (a) the registering court; (b) its provisional
-- order confirmed abroad "and notice of the confirmation is received"; or (c) a court in the reciprocating country "and notice of the
-- revocation is received". (2): also where the officer "is of the opinion that the payer ... has ceased to reside within the
-- jurisdiction of that court", sending the copy to the Minister.
GIVEN `revoked by the registering court outright` IS A BOOLEAN, `revoked abroad or by a confirmed provisional order` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `notice received by the registering court` IS A BOOLEAN, `officer thinks the payer has left the jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the registration must be cancelled` IF
        `revoked by the registering court outright`
    OR  (`revoked abroad or by a confirmed provisional order` AND `notice received by the registering court`)
    OR  `officer thinks the payer has left the jurisdiction`

§§ `14(3) -- compensating a witness`

-- s 14(3): where "any person, not being the payer or the payee under the maintenance order to which the proceedings in question
-- relate, is required by virtue of this section to give evidence", the court "may order" payment out of moneys provided by
-- Parliament to compensate "for the expense, trouble or loss of time".
GIVEN `required to give evidence for foreign proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN, `is the payer` IS A BOOLEAN, `is the payee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the court may compensate the witness` IF
        `required to give evidence for foreign proceedings`
    AND (NOT `is the payer`)
    AND (NOT `is the payee`)

§§ `16(2), (5) -- converting a foreign-currency order`

-- s 16(2): an order in a foreign currency is treated "as from the relevant date" as requiring the Singapore-dollar equivalent "on the
-- basis of the rate of exchange prevailing at that date". (5): "the relevant date" means "(a) ... the date on which the order first
-- becomes a registered order or (if earlier) the date on which it is confirmed by a court in Singapore; and (b) in relation to a
-- registered order which has been varied -- the date on which the last order varying that order is registered ... or (if earlier)
-- the date on which the last order varying that order is confirmed by such a court". (4): a bank officer's certificate is evidence
-- of the rate.
GIVEN `day first registered` IS A NUMBER, `confirmed in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN, `day confirmed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the relevant date for an unvaried order` MEANS
    IF `confirmed in Singapore` THEN `the earlier of` `day first registered` `day confirmed` ELSE `day first registered`

GIVEN `day last variation registered` IS A NUMBER, `last variation confirmed in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN, `day last variation confirmed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the relevant date for a varied order` MEANS
    IF `last variation confirmed in Singapore`
    THEN `the earlier of` `day last variation registered` `day last variation confirmed`
    ELSE `day last variation registered`

GIVEN `foreign-currency sum` IS A NUMBER, `Singapore dollars per unit at the relevant date` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Singapore-dollar sum` MEANS
    `foreign-currency sum` TIMES `Singapore dollars per unit at the relevant date`
